3	/**
4	 * Nxeon node-agent — see docs/DOCUMENTATION.md's "Multi-node synergy" section
5	 * for the full design. Runs on every NON-PRIMARY compute node. Gives the
6	 * primary's worker a narrow, token-authenticated way to touch this node's own
7	 * NAT table and cloud-init snippet storage — the two host-level operations
8	 * the worker cannot reach any other way once it isn't running on this box.
9	 *
10	 * DELIBERATELY plain, dependency-free JavaScript (Node built-ins only: http,
11	 * https, fs, child_process, crypto, url) — this ONE file is copied to a
12	 * freshly onboarded node that has no npm packages, no copy of this repo, and
13	 * should need neither. No database access, no Proxmox API token, nothing
14	 * beyond what these operations need — a leaked token's blast radius is NAT
15	 * rules and cloud-init snippets for this one node, never a shell, never data.
16	 *
17	 * AUTH: every request must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, checked by
18	 * constant-time comparison against NXEON_AGENT_TOKEN (env, sourced from
19	 * /etc/nxeon/node-agent.env — the only copy of the plaintext token on this
20	 * machine; the primary's copy is encrypted at rest, see lib/node-agent.ts).
21	 * Network exposure is ADDITIONALLY restricted by this node's own firewall to
22	 * the primary's public IP only (see onboard-node.sh's agent-allow rule) — the
23	 * token is defense in depth on top of that, not the only gate.
24	 *
25	 * TRANSPORT: HTTPS with a self-signed cert generated once at onboard time
26	 * (openssl, no CA involved). The primary connects with certificate
27	 * verification disabled — the SAME trust model this codebase already uses to
28	 * reach this node's own Proxmox API (lib/proxmox.ts's insecureAgent) — which
29	 * still encrypts the token on the wire without needing a CA-issued cert for a
30	 * bare IP with no public DNS name.
31	 *
32	 * Run directly: node node-agent/index.js
33	 * As a service: deploy/nxeon-node-agent.service (installed by onboard-node.sh)
34	 */
